<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan copper imports up 18.6 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan copper imports up 18.6 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in January rose to 27,526 tonnes, up 18.6 percent from 23,217 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Jan 96	  Dec 96	 Jan 95</p>
<p> Total	    27,526	  28,988	 23,217</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	     9,378	  13,198	 11,247</p>
<p> U.S.		3,536	   3,448	  4,795</p>
<p> Zambia	    5,860	   2,686	  1,477</p>
<p>Imports in calendar 1996 were 360,019 tonnes, down 7.6 percent from 389,760 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
